  "term": "disorientation",
  "definition": "Disorientation is a loss of correct direction in which an individual moves away from its natural route instead of toward the intended destination. In the source context, it refers to sea turtle hatchlings being drawn off the path to the ocean, often by artificial light that interferes with normal navigation cues.",
